---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';

const effectiveDate = 'October 13, 2026';
---

<Base
	title="Privacy Policy | Digital Honeycomb"
	description="How Digital Honeycomb collects, uses and protects information on digitalhoneycomb.com."
>
	<SiteHeader />

	<main class="section">
		<article class="container prose">
			<span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="prose-meta">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>

			<p>
				This policy explains what information Digital Honeycomb ("we," "us") collects when you visit
				digitalhoneycomb.com, how we use it, and the choices you have.
			</p>

			<h2>Information we collect</h2>
			<h3>Information you give us</h3>
			<p>
				When you send us a message through the contact form, we collect your name, email address and message,
				and, if you choose to provide them, your company and the service you're interested in.
			</p>
			<h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
			<p>
				This site does not use analytics or advertising cookies. Our hosting provider may record standard server
				logs, including IP addresses, for security and reliability.
			</p>

			<h2>How we use information</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>To reply to your message and discuss the services you asked about.</li>
				<li>To keep the site secure and prevent abuse.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for third-party advertising.</p>

			<h2>Service providers</h2>
			<p>We rely on a small number of providers to run this site. They process information on our behalf:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong>: website hosting.</li>
				<li><strong>Supabase</strong>: secure storage of contact form messages.</li>
				<li><strong>Resend</strong>: delivery of internal notification emails about new messages.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				We may also disclose information if required by law, or to protect the rights, safety and security of
				Digital Honeycomb, our clients or others.
			</p>

			<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
			<p>
				We keep contact form messages for as long as we need them to respond to you and to maintain a record of
				our conversation, or until you ask us to remove them.
			</p>

			<h2>Your choices</h2>
			<p>
				To see, update or delete the information you've sent us, <a href="/#contact">send us a message</a> and
				we'll take care of it. Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights to access, correct or
				delete your personal information, and we'll respond to any such request.
			</p>

			<h2>Security</h2>
			<p>
				We use reasonable safeguards to protect your information. Messages can be sent from the website but
				cannot be read back through it. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, however.
			</p>

			<h2>Children</h2>
			<p>This site is intended for businesses. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.</p>

			<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>If we update this policy, we'll post the new version here and change the effective date above.</p>
		</article>
	</main>

	<SiteFooter />
</Base>
